      "innovation": "Span-based dynamic convolution (SDConv) module: applies dynamic convolution over spans of the input sequence to efficiently capture local context, differing from standard self-attention which computes global pairwise interactions and is computationally heavy for local patterns; Bottleneck structure: projects input embeddings to a lower-dimensional space (d/γ) for self-attention and reduces the number of attention heads by ratio γ, largely saving computation cost within self-attention and forcing heads to yield more compact and useful attention information compared to the original transformer architecture; Grouped linear (GL) operator: applies a grouped linear operation to the feed-forward module in a grouped manner, which is more efficient than the fully connected layer and costs negligible performance drop while maintaining representation power and reducing parameters.",
